020 crash, 33% in the 2022 bear market and 70% in 2008."],"val":["The price sits above its blended-model fair value of $161 (margin of safety -20%), so there is no valuation cushion.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 21%), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks cheap against Technology peers: P/E 9.8 vs 27.4 and EV/EBITDA 7.5 vs 17.1 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 178% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are thin: an FCF yield of -0.4% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 6.5% (vs the 8% bar).","The 4 covering analysts target $216 on average, 12% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 12% earns above the cost of capital of 8.7%, but the 4pp spread is short of the 7pp moat bar; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.40).","It runs a 12% gross margin and burns cash (FCF margin -0%).","Earnings quality is a concern: cash conversion of only 0.11x.","ROE of 9% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (4.4x equity multiplier)."],"hlth":["Leverage is moderate at 2.9x net debt to EBITDA ($306.5M of cash against $3.1B of debt), above the 1.5x gate."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at -6.0% over 3 years, 1.5% over 5 years and 2.9% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating.","At current returns, reinvesting 100% of profits supports about 12.4% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Capex runs only 0.7x depreciation (0.3% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown.","Its Rule of 40 score is 1, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.6%), and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Insiders have only sold over the past year (7 sales, net $10.8M sold).","Shareholder yield is a modest 1.7% (1.7% in buybacks).","The share count has shrunk 7.9% a year over five years, steadily raisi